bioterrorism-by-belowabsolutezero (1.0+1-0ddebs7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Changes prepared with Claude Opus 5.5
  * debian/patches : 02_align_stack_for_modern_libraries.patch, align
    the stack on 16 bytes before each library call (crashed at start
    with sdl12-compat/SDL2)
  * debian/patches : 03_clean_version_and_private_tmpfile.patch, build
    the upstream clean version (proper exit, restores the screen) and
    unpack it with mktemp instead of /tmp/a
  * debian/patches : 04_play_silence_after_the_music.patch, fix a crash
    around 46 s when the audio callback runs faster than real time
  * debian/patches : 05_reload_gl_arguments.patch, pass the program again
    to glLinkProgram/glUseProgram (the nvidia driver overwrites it, only
    a red fade was displayed)
  * debian/patches : 06_standard_glsl.patch, valid GLSL so that the
    shader also compiles with Mesa
  * debian/control : depend on libsdl1.2debian and libgl1 (libsdl1.2-
    compat is not available on Ubuntu 26.04 and Debian 14), better
    description
  * removed the launcher script and its manual page, the .desktop file
    already starts the intro directly
  * debian/resources : added the missing icon (screenshot from
    pouet.net)
  * debian/copyright : no license found upstream, public-domain
    (probably freeware)
  * debian/bioterrorism-by-belowabsolutezero.6.md : updated manual page

 -- Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:44:41 +0100

